reate a Planetary Background for a world other than those given here. To do so, the Gamemaster should choose three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," that are relevant to the planet's history, culture, or reputation. In addition, if the planet is home to a native ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", add the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Language"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Language"}," of that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," to the Background as a Bonus Language. If the planet has no natives, the Gamemaster instead should choose a common trade language (such as Bocce or Sy Bisti) or High Galactic. The latter language is especially appropriate for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Worlds"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Worlds?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and planets that pride themselves on their prestige.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
